<title>USA: Tucson Elec., Ariz., repriced, ylds 7.125 in 2032.</title>
<headline>Tucson Elec., Ariz., repriced, ylds 7.125 in 2032.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co., Inc. said Thursday it repriced Tucson Electric Power Co. $132 million bond deal, with a top yield of 7.125 percent in 2032</p>
<p>TUCSON ELECTRIC POWER COMPANY POLLUTION</p>
<p>RE: $131,810,000*</p>
<p>CONTROL REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE REPRICING.</p>
<p>					    80,410,000*</p>
<p>		   CITY OF FARMINGTON, NEW MEXICO POLLUTION</p>
<p>			 CONTROL REVENUE BONDS 1997 SERIES A</p>
<p>		(TUCSON ELECTRIC POWER COMPANY SAN JUAN PROJECT)</p>
<p>					  NON AMT</p>
<p>MOODY'S: B2		    S&amp;P: B-		    FITCH: B+</p>
<p>DATED: 04/01/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 10/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>10/01/2020	     80,410M    6.95  %</p>
